<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paul von Hindenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1847">1847</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul von Hindenburg was a German field marshal and president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a> from 1925 to 1934. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erich-ludendorff">Erich Ludendorff</a> he won the Battle of Tannenberg in 1914 and commanded in the east, where the occupied Ober Ost was named after his post, before directing the whole German war effort. As president he appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> chancellor in January 1933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paul-von-hindenburg.jpg" alt="Paul von Hindenburg" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-C06886,_Paul_v._Hindenburg_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
